   "instrument_id": "EO:10775",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"The Federal Aviation Agency regulations of July 12, 1961 (Airspace Docket No. 60-LA-119, 26 FR 6233) that the Federal Register disposition note says repealed this order are not held; their text is needed to establish what they repealed and on what date, together with whether they name Executive Order 10633 or this order.\", \"No held instrument or record ends the airspace reservation over the Las Vegas Project established by Executive Order 10633 (needed: a later executive order, Civil Aeronautics Board or Federal Aviation Agency regulation or order, or other dated instrument that revoked, superseded or discontinued the reservation, or the held text of the Federal Aviation Act of 1958 with an analysis of whether it extinguished the reservation).\", \"Executive Order 10633's own terms and later history are not in the packet; the parent's end date governs this amendment's first end.\"]"
  },
  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:10792",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "Independent review did not uphold this version: [{\"field\": \"operative_clauses[EO:10792#whole].first_end.date (leave-policy direction) and whole_order_end.date\", \"claim_says\": \"1958-12-26, the leave direction 'read as tied to the excused day', broader reading disclosed\", \"source_says\": \"The second paragraph directs agency heads to adopt a liberal annual-leave policy for employees 'who wish to take such leave over the holiday period'. The order does not equate the holiday period with Friday, December 26, 1958 (all employees are already excused that day and Christmas is a holiday, so the direction has its effect on other days), and no held source dates the period's end. The claim itself admits 'no held text fixes' the end and describes the broader reading as running to the end of the Christmas and New Year period.\"}]"
