   "reason": "Independent review did not uphold this version: [{\"field\": \"operative_clauses[EO:10825#sec4b].first_end.date\", \"claim_says\": \"1959-07-03 (close of July 3, 1959): the request 'concerns only that day'\", \"source_says\": \"The held fragment of section 4 requests agency heads to arrange affairs to excuse employees on that day 'or to grant compensatory time m / reof' (in lieu thereof) without additional appropriations. Compensatory time in lieu of an excused day is by nature given on another, later day, and the order states no deadline for it. No held source shows the request ended at the close of July 3, 1959; the endpoint has no reason.\"}, {\"field\": \"operative_clauses[EO:10825#sec1].first_end.date\", \"claim_says\": \"1959-07-03; subsection (b) workday 'ends with it'\", \"source_says\": \"Section 1(b) excuses employees from an entire workday that 'commences on July 2 or July 3, 1959' and covers portions of two calendar days including July 3; a workday commencing July 3 runs into July 4, 1959, so the excusal can operate after the close of July 3.\"}, {\"field\": \"whole_order_end\", \"claim_says\": \"1960-06-30, the latest clause end\", \"source_says\": \"Because the compensatory-time request has no established end, the latest first end among the clauses (and so the whole-order end) is not established by the held sources.\"}]"
